. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         /*      Inclusion/exclusion criteria according to TEAM's PAP: 
>         1. Include individuals >18 years with one child only  [age>18&sumkids
> ==1]
>         2. Exclude homosexuals (who could potentially choose their child's ge
> nder)
>         */      
. 
. *Deviations from PAP
.         *We said "we would append observations from 2016 and 2017 and keep th
> e first time an individual appeared", but we ended up using only 2018.
.         *In PAP we proposed to use an Equality index using Bhp_504_q56, Bhp_5
> 05_q56 Bhp_506_q56, bhp_507_q56, and hp_508_q56 (named plj0621 plj0622 plj062
> 3 plj0624 plj0625 in the actual dataset) but later realized it was only asked
>  to immigrants
.         *We do not include "urban/rural" nor "religious_freq", as stated in t
> he PAP, because of the high number of missing observations found
.         
.                 gen sample=(age>18 & sumkids==1 & age_child>0 & heterosexual!
> =0) // We set age_child>0 because apparently in the 5% data there are "yet to
>  become parents" observations that at the moment of being surveyed have imput
> ed an age of the child that occurs in the future, so when we build the child'
> s age, it's a negative number. 

.                 
